  </div>
  <p>
    In April 2024, on a weekend on Catalina Island, dinner was at <strong>Bluewater Grill</strong> on the Avalon
    waterfront: seared scallops in a red pepper sauce.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'bluewater-scallops.webp'} alt="Three seared scallops on a long plate with red pepper sauce and a drizzle of cream." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Scallops, Bluewater Grill, Avalon, April 20, 2024.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    Three days later, <strong>Nobu</strong> on La Cienega: yellowtail with jalapeño, shishito peppers and wagyu tacos.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'nobu-yellowtail-r.webp'} alt="Thin slices of yellowtail with jalapeño in ponzu, arranged in a star." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Yellowtail jalapeño, Nobu, April 23, 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'nobu-tacos-r.webp'} alt="Blistered shishito peppers above a slate of small tacos." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Shishitos and wagyu tacos.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    April 2025 was beef twice in one week. <strong>NIKU X</strong>, on the second floor of the Wilshire Grand
    downtown, brings out a tomahawk and carves it at the table.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'nikux-tomahawk.webp'} alt="A whole grilled tomahawk steak with its long bone on a wooden board." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The tomahawk, NIKU X, April 19, 2025.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'nikux-sliced.webp'} alt="Sliced steak and the carved bone on a round black plate." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Carved.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    Four days later, <strong>Manpuku</strong> in Costa Mesa was Japanese yakiniku: marbled wagyu on a charcoal grill.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'manpuku-grill.webp'} alt="Slices of marbled wagyu on a round grill over glowing charcoal." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Manpuku, Costa Mesa, April 23, 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    Then three more that summer. <strong>Agora Churrascaria</strong> in Irvine in May, where the waiters keep bringing
    meat on skewers until you turn your card over. <strong>Splashes</strong>, at the Surf &amp; Sand in Laguna Beach, in
    June.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'agora.webp'} alt="A plate of carved steak, sausage and sides with a basket of cheese bread." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Agora Churrascaria, Irvine, May 2025.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'splashes.webp'} alt="Four small plated courses on a white tablecloth." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Splashes, Laguna Beach, June 18, 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    And <strong>Geoffrey's</strong> in Malibu at the end of June: paella on a terrace above the Pacific Coast Highway.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'geoffreys-paella.webp'} alt="A plate of seafood paella with shrimp and mussels." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Paella, Geoffrey's, Malibu, June 29, 2025.</figcaption></figure>
